<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balthasar von Dernbach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1548">1548</a>–<a href="/years/1606">1606</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balthasar von Dernbach was prince-abbot of Fulda from 1570 to 1606. A determined Counter-Reformer, he brought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a> and pressed his Protestant subjects to return to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a>, which led the chapter and the knights to depose him in 1576. Restored by imperial judgement in 1602, he resumed his campaign until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/balthasar-von-dernbach.jpg" alt="Balthasar von Dernbach" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dernbach_Ba_2001.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
